<section class="section">
  <div class="container split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">What the compliance engine does</p>
      <h2>One requirements engine, configured per sector.</h2>
      <p>Every sector answers to a different set of authorities. An oil and gas operator tracks permit conditions, integrity intervals, and spill prevention plans. A utility tracks discharge limits, water quality sampling, and capital reporting to a council. A defense installation tracks property accountability and self-inspection cycles. An infrastructure owner tracks bridge inspection intervals and federal funding conditions across every jurisdiction its assets sit in.</p>
      <p>The engine underneath is the same. Every asset record, inspection, and form maps to the specific citation it satisfies — not a generic compliance tag.</p>
    </div>
